Z||000004||K2m4||12-21-2001||10:30 AM||||Hey dude its cheaper to buy the whole starter /starter solenoid package than it is to buy just the solenoid. NAPA it was actually more expensive to buy the solenoid alone. Anyhow you have to remove the starter anyway you might as well replace the whole sh*t and kabootle in one shot. Just my .02 cents<P><P>------------------<BR>Kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||12-21-2001||11:20 AM||||Before you jump into changing the starter, are you sure that's where the problem lies?<BR>If your car is an automatic, there is a park/neutral switch that may be out of adjustment or bad.  It's on the transmission.  If you have a stick shift, there is a start safety switch on the clutch pedal.  These also have been known to cause problems.  If you're not even getting a click out of the solonoid, I'd tend to look at these switches, or possibly the ignition switch before jumping into a starter change.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||4
